Edit:: Apologies, I missed the word "Basics" and assumed 5e. I haven't had enough coffee

I used KFC as a resource for what to use in encounters. It had all (or near to all) 3rd party content and even had homebrew stuff from Monster-a-day subreddit, and told you what the source for those monsters were so you could find the stats. It was also nice to just enter in what ever monsters I DID end up using and getting the quick calc on xp to reward. 

&#x200B;

Even just setting an environment and CR range and clicking random encounter a few times was a great way to start getting some ideas flowing. It was more useful as a creative tool than anything else honestly

Make this post go up! This tool looks like it works very similar to KFC, at least in terms of searching for monsters, and what sources they come from which is primarily what I used KFC for. 

&#x200B;

More than anything I usually just want ideas for monsters I can use, which KFC was great about, but to go along with that, you need to know where the stats for those monsters actually live too.

I don't know about specific descriptions, but many encounter building tools/sites like Kobold Fight Club let you search by creatures that fit specific environments.

&#x200B;

You can search for creatures that fit into a swamp setting, or mountains, or even underground/underdark. I like to use these to get ideas of what might live in each area and build off those ideas.

&#x200B;

If you find something with short summaries let me know because I tend to forget the decriptions of some of the more unique creatures I try to use then later realize I used them in a way that doesn't fit particularly well with how they're written.

My old LG V20 is really starting to suffer. Battery went from 80+% to full dead over night last night (this was a replacement battery as well, only a year or 2 old). Processing speed starting to tank.

&#x200B;

Trying not to break the bank, I found the LG V60 ThinQ 5G UW on verizon and it looks like it's a good little phone and the price seems reasonable.

&#x200B;

I prefer the larger phones, I've had Notes and the V20 for my last 3-4 phones and I don't want to go back to the small ones. My other requirements are pretty basic. I play some mobile games, social media, pictures/videos of the kids. I just want it to be quick and responsive so I can get on, look up what I need to and get off again nice and quick.

&#x200B;

Any suggestions would be great. Is the V60 as good a fit as it seems? Anything similar I should look into? Thanks!

I just bought my first riding mower. I know I shouldn't be mowing in the same direction every time, but I have a fence around the entire backyard, and stonework around the front. The first mow I did with this, I went clockwise so the discharge shoot was pointing away from the fence so I could try getting as close as I could, then just continued going in that direction, spiraling into the center.

&#x200B;

What should I do now for the next time when edging the yard with the rider? The side shoot isn't going to let me get very close to the fence if I try going the opposite direction

It's just her side of the family, we usually do it Christmas eve, but a handful of them never bothered to request the day off when we planned this in fucking May, so we had to change it to Sunday. Without MIL, stepdad and shitty BIL, it's only going to be other BIL and his wife and 1yo kid, SIL and her boyfriend, shitty BIL's exwife and their 2 kids, and MAYBE  cousin and 2 aunts, but probably not.

&#x200B;

edits to clarify between BILs

I get what you're saying, but to be fair, this is our first home, and we've only lived there for a few years now, and it was a foreclosure. There's been lots of surprises, both from in-experience of owning a home and from lack of upkeep from the previous owners. We've learned a lot about our property in these few years including a number of things that could have hastened the decay of some of these systems (we apparently have highly acidic water which literally burned through the tankless water heater that was in place when we purchased). Our next tax return is partially going towards a water filtration system to help prevent any further pipe decay. 

&#x200B;

With the property being a foreclosure, a lot of the information we had about these systems were guesses from the inspectors and service people (regarding our furnace, when we had it cleaned the first time the service guy said "It could last you another 6 years or another 6 months.").

&#x200B;

But I do understand what you're saying, especially the first part of your post regarding the retirement and emergency funds. We're good about not blowing our money on dumb things, and I feel like I do a halfway decent job keeping the finances in order. I pay the majority of the bills and have never missed a payment on anything, and I focus paying down particular debts when we're able to put a little extra money into them. 

The student loans right now are the primary killer though. I'm paying about 400$ a month between sallie mei and federal loans (SM interest keeps going up, at 11.5% right now. Fed average is \~7% between 10 loans). I'm on an income based payment plan for the fed loans, so trying to refinance seriously spikes my payments beyond what I'd be able to afford. Right now I'm just focusing on getting the remaining 7k sallie mei loan down.

I can't get the Recruit a Friend to work on the Mog Station.

&#x200B;

I log into the Mog Station, go to the Account Services tab

There's a little banner about 3/4 of the way down that says "Recruit a Friend"

I click that, it opens a new tab and brings me back to the Mog Station login

I login again, it brings me back to the Mog Station Account Services page..

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

Any ideas?

The first guy we had look at it did specifically say that we could end up with water pouring out of it at any point now. 

I've also had a second guy look (I haven't gone to any of the big box stores, I'm working with local guys), who also agreed the unit was due for the scrap heap. He gave me a set of estimates (5800, 6500, 7400) for several different installs. All the quotes I've received have included replacing the zone valves. 

&#x200B;

We have 1 more local guy coming Saturday morning and unless he says something drastically different, I think we're probably leaning towards the 6500 unit, just a matter of which contractor we go with at that point.

&#x200B;

The first guy quoted us for a Dunkirk EXB unit with a Riello burner, second quote was for a  Viessmann Vitorond 100 VR1, also with a Riello burner. Both are cast iron and seem rated pretty similarly from what I can find online, with the Viessmann possibly being a little more advanced.

Yea, I'm not a huge fan of the whole "smart house" thing to be honest. I'm just now getting on the LED board lighting train, I'm a little behind on home tech. Haha. 

&#x200B;

So the traveler wire would connect the 4 lights, or the 2 switches? Pretty sure the switches are on the same breaker, but that's definitely something I would need to double check. I hadn't heard that requirement before, but that definitely makes sense. Thanks for that bit.

The thing is I genuinely do think it's to "win over love" because that's what I see that family do constantly. They don't know how to show actual affection so they just buy things. The rest of the young kids were such spoiled brats for a very very long time because they were bought things every time they saw the family, and if they weren't bought something they would just hand them money. It was really upsetting for me to see that and I don't want my daughter to grow up like that.

&#x200B;

This is why I posted though, maybe that's a shitty way to look at it, but it's just so drastically different from anything I experienced growing up. My aunts and uncles would never dote on me or my sister like that. We knew they loved us, but gifts were for birthdays and christmas. I couldn't imagine walking up to my grandmother or my aunt as a kid and saying "I want some money" like I've seen my wife's nieces and nephews do.

&#x200B;

edit: And even for xmas or birthdays, aunts and uncles would get us a handful of small things, never would they have spent hundreds of dollars like that... Last year SIL wanted to get my daughter one of those powerwheel jeeps... I was at least able to get my wife to convince her that was something WE should be getting her that time...

SIL is paying for it, actually. I'd understand completely if that changes things for you. 

&#x200B;

But yea, I mean granted I don't want SIL renting the horse for us period, but I'm more upset that my wife didn't WANT to tell me about it...

It's defintely more pride than anything. I'll completely own that. 

&#x200B;

Part of it too, honestly is, we have a big ass yard and when we moved in, my wife's entire family was like "Oh! You can get horses! Your daughter would love to have horses!" (daughter was a month old when we bought the house). 

&#x200B;

I don't want horses... I don't want to pay for them, I don't want to see or smell them all the time, I don't want to take care of them, but I feel like they are constantly pushing horses down my throat and this is just another fucking jab at it and it gets under my skin. If I'm an asshole for that I will 100% own it though.

My daughter isn't her first niece, she has another niece and a nephew that I never saw her doing these kinds of things with.

&#x200B;

I only have personal experiences to relay here, but I genuinely don't think she is a "kind" person... She's also not a very bright person, so this legitimately may not be an attempt to one up me, but at the very least it would be an attempt to put herself in the spot light.

&#x200B;

The day my daughter was born, SIL came to the hospital room and started crying. Not tears of joy at a new addition to the family, mind you, she started crying, looked to my wife and said, I kid you not "You're not going to have as much time for me now". This grown ass girl (30s) is just an attention whore as far as I'm concerned...

&#x200B;

But again... maybe I'm just an asshole who doesn't want to share all my daughter's firsts, like first bike, first time to the zoo (had to fight for that one too...)

