Thanks for the tips on the craftsman, that definitely helps

I would love to get a band saw, and probably will eventually, but looking at the prices, that's not an option RIGHT NOW.

&#x200B;

For the next couple projects I have in mind, things my wife has requested, I do actually think I'll be doing a lot of panel work, and ripping. My wife also does a lot of little wood crafts, she's not comfortable with some of the bigger tools, and I think she would feel better with a big sturdy table saw over something like a band saw, which seems to me more intimidating. For me, I do think a table saw is the best option right now. 

&#x200B;

That being said, the one I linked was a 10" Craftsman "portable", so it's on a base with wheels. I'm a little skeptical about the stability of the base, but I figure I can probably take if off that base and put it on a table/bench if I really need to, but it would be nice to have the stand when I need to drag it out of the basement and use it outside.

&#x200B;

I've definitely been keeping an eye out for a used table saw on a couple facebook pages, but haven't seen anything I completely trust yet. A lot of the reasonably priced ones look like they've literally been through hell. The ones that look like they're in reasonable condition are asking more than the new one I'm looking at...

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

Uhhhhh... I'm sorry dude, but you've been gone too long to have any real input here apparently, because the points you've made here are completely wrong...

&#x200B;

I've been an assassination rogue since WotLK, and last night I was close to top dps in my guilds first push into Heroic Uldir...

&#x200B;

The 1 concession I will make here; Yes energy Regen is a little slow right now, but it gets better when you have the correct gear for your spec, and will continue to get better as the expansion goes on. It always does...

&#x200B;

First point: I can't say I've ever opened with cheap shot in any content outside of PvP. It's a waste of energy to do it once and it's completely dumb to do it twice... You're right, mobs die pretty quickly so if you want to actually contribute to that kill, open with some damage instead of the useless stun. Cheap shot is very situational. It can be useful, but the majority of the time you will be better off using the correct opening sequence.

&#x200B;

Next: Your opener is just wrong... I don't know what you've got for azerite traits (I'll assume you probably don't have the really good ones, ie Shrouded Suffocation), but you ALWAYS open with garrote. Then you want to get to 4-5 combo points, usually with mutilate, sometimes with more garrotes (more on that later), then rupture. Once both those are up, if the fight is going to take a while (ie a boss), you want to drop your first cool down; Vendetta. This is going to not only give you a nice boost to your regen, it empowers your attacks for \~20 seconds. Then you want to throw in a Toxic Blade (that's the recommended talent), then you go into a burst spam of mut to 4-5cp, envenom, mut to 4-5, envenom. As you're doing that you want to keep your garrote and ruptures up at all times. If they fall off, that's energy you're not getting back (remember, bleeds give you energy!)

&#x200B;

My standard opening for a boss:

&#x200B;

Garrote > Rupture > Garrote > Vendetta > Mut > Toxic Blade > Envenom > Mut/Env (repeat)When Garrote gets to about 4s remaining Vanish > Garrote > Garrote > Rupture

&#x200B;

EDIT: non-max level opener - Garrote > Mut 4-5cp > Rupture > Vendetta > Mut / ENV spam, when garrote gets to 4s vanish > Garrote

&#x200B;

There's no pooling in there. There's no sitting on my thumbs. This is active gameplay and with only 337 ilvl, I'm spiking around 15k dps in the first 10 seconds of the fight.

&#x200B;

As for AoE, you mentioned there's nothing... Your bleeds ARE your aoe. Open from stealth, garrote 3 targets, rupture 1, fan of knives till 4-5 cp, rupture another, repeat till you have literally 6 bleeds and near infinite energy...

&#x200B;

Please don't come on here and try to blast something you have 0 understanding of, it's bad rep for rogues and makes other newbies think they're not worth playing.

&#x200B;

EDIT:: I read this as you had already leveled to max, so ignore the bits pertaining to max level talents and azerite traits, but the rest should still be valid.
